2. The strongest proof that C is causing the lag

Don't start with CPU/RAM. Start with timestamps.

During an application-lag event, collect these four things:

Evidence	What you want to see
Application latency	Latency increases at T1
C replication lag	C's lag increases at/just before T1
C resources	CPU/disk/cache/IO wait increases at same time
Primary flow control	isLagged=true, reduced targetRateLimit, increased ticket acquisition time

The most convincing pattern would be:

C resource saturation → C replication falls behind → majority commit lag increases → flow control activates → primary write throughput is throttled → application latency increases.
That is considerably stronger evidence than simply observing "C has less CPU/RAM."

MongoDB's replSetGetStatus gives you optimeDate, optimeWrittenDate, lastAppliedWallTime, syncSourceHost, and pingMs, which are exactly the fields I would use to establish this relationship.



